  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q17-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Show that the sum of $2n-1$ consecutive integers is divisible by $2n-1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^{2n-1}(k+i)=(2n-1)(k+n)$.\n\nThe sum is an integer multiple of $2n-1$.",
      "worked": "Let the integers be $k+1,k+2,\\ldots,k+2n-1$, where $k$ is an integer and $n$ is a positive integer.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum_{i=1}^{2n-1}(k+i)&=(2n-1)k+\\sum_{i=1}^{2n-1}i\\\\\\sum_{i=1}^{2n-1}(k+i)&=(2n-1)k+\\frac{(2n-1)(2n)}{2}\\\\\\sum_{i=1}^{2n-1}(k+i)&=(2n-1)k+n(2n-1)\\\\\\sum_{i=1}^{2n-1}(k+i)&=(2n-1)(k+n).\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $k+n$ is an integer, the sum is divisible by $2n-1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
